# Titles and descriptions of the commands (blueprint 10.1). Quick search and the CLI show them.

command-projects-list-title = Show projects
command-projects-list-description = Lists the registered projects with their newest scan.
command-projects-add-title = Add project
command-projects-add-description = Registers a folder or a Git repository as a project and scans it.
command-projects-rescan-title = Scan project again
command-projects-rescan-description = Scans a project again; only changed files are read if it was scanned before.
command-explorer-outline-title = Show structure
command-explorer-outline-description = Lists the layers, namespaces and types of the newest scan.
command-explorer-symbol-title = Show symbol
command-explorer-symbol-description = Shows one type or member with its metrics and members.
command-search-query-title = Search symbols
command-search-query-description = Searches the names of the types and members of the newest scan.
command-status-info-title = Show status
command-status-info-description = Shows the start time and the memory of the program.
command-explorer-source-title = Show source
command-explorer-source-description = Shows the lines of the declaration of a type or member, read from the project folder.
